    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I'm Dr. Smith. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Hi Dr. Smith. Um, well, my supervisor basically made me come in. He says it's becoming a huge safety problem at work because I keep leaving my station, or like, I'll just be popping up during our shift meetings when everybody's supposed to stay put. I just take off before I even think about it, you know? \n\nBut honestly, if they want to talk about safety problems, they really need to look at Gary. He drives the forklift on the loading dock and he literally almost backed into a massive stack of pallets yesterday because he was looking at his phone. I swear, they let him get away with everything just because he's been there forever. I told my friend who works at the Amazon warehouse about it, and she said they'd fire him on the spot over there. She makes way better money than me, too, plus they get better benefits. I should probably just apply there, honestly, it's only like a ten-minute drive from my apartment. \n\nBut yeah, anyway, my boss is mad because I keep getting out of my seat and walking off.",
