    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from the trouble with sitting still, do you often find that you make careless mistakes or have a hard time staying focused on tasks that aren't particularly interesting to you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Oh, definitely. Like, when I'm doing the inventory logs at work, or reading through the CNC training pages they give us, I really do start out trying to pay attention. But after just a few minutes, the numbers and words just start to blur together, and I have to keep going back over the same page because I realize I didn't take any of it in. \n\nIt really doesn't help that they make us do the training on these super old tablets with totally shattered screens. My phone screen is actually cracked right now, too. I dropped it in the Target parking lot last week because I was trying to balance my keys and this giant iced coffee at the same time. It was one of those brown sugar oat milk shaken espressos? They are so good, but they're getting ridiculously expensive now. I swear it was almost seven dollars just for a coffee! My roommate makes hers at home with this little frother wand she bought off TikTok shop, but I just don't have the patience to stand there and make it myself in the morning. Plus, I heard TikTok shop is super sketchy anyway, like people get their credit card info stolen on there all the time. I'd rather just go to the drive-thru, even if it costs more. \n\nBut um... wait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, focusing on stuff. Yeah, if it's boring like the inventory logs, my brain just kind of checks out completely.",
