    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you find that you frequently lose things like your keys, wallet, or paperwork, or do you often find yourself becoming easily distracted by things going on around you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S008",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, the distraction thing is huge. Like, when I'm on the line at work? Literally just one beep from another machine, or if somebody walks past with a pallet jack, my eyes and my whole brain just get completely pulled away from what I'm doing. And I know I'm supposed to just stay on my own station and focus, but I just can't help looking. \n\nThose pallet jacks are so loud, too. They have these hard wheels that just grind on the concrete all day. My uncle actually used to work in concrete. He poured driveways and patios and stuff, but he messed up his back really bad doing it. He had to get this crazy surgery where they put all these metal screws in his spine. I saw the X-ray on his Facebook once and it literally looked like he swallowed a bunch of hardware from Home Depot. I actually love going to Home Depot, honestly. It always smells so good in there, like fresh sawdust and plants. I bought a little succulent there last month but I already killed it because I kept forgetting to water it. Or maybe I watered it too much? I can never remember what you're supposed to do with those things. People say they're impossible to kill but I guess I proved them wrong. \n\nBut um... wait, what were you asking me? Oh, losing things! Yeah, I mean I do lose my keys all the time, but the distraction thing on the line is definitely the biggest issue.",
