    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "When you think about the problems you've had at school and work, would you say the bigger issue is that you have trouble focusing and finishing tasks, or is it more that you act without thinking and have trouble staying still?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Honestly, it's definitely the acting without thinking and not being able to sit still. Like, I just feel this constant need to be moving or doing something, and I'll just jump up or blurt something out before my brain even catches up. \n\nIt's kind of like when I go grocery shopping. I'll go in for, like, milk and bread, and then suddenly I'm in the aisle with the baking stuff and I'm throwing three boxes of brownie mix in my cart because I just decided right then that I need to make brownies. Which I never end up doing, by the way. I still have a box of red velvet cake mix in my pantry from like, six months ago. Red velvet is so weird if you think about it. It's just chocolate cake with a ton of red food coloring, right? But people go crazy for it. My sister had a red velvet wedding cake and it was honestly kind of dry. The frosting was good though, it was that cream cheese kind. I could probably just eat a tub of cream cheese frosting with a spoon. \n\nBut um, yeah, definitely the moving around and acting on impulse. The focus thing is bad too, but the physical part of it gets me in trouble way more.",
